cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use eaftox in your research, please cite this software."
type: software
title: "eaftox: Browser-based EAF converter with audio segmentation"
authors:
  - family-names: Shimoji
    given-names: Michinori
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-10-25'
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23644511
license: MIT
url: "https://michinorishimoji.github.io/eaftox/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MichinoriShimoji/eaftox"
abstract: >-
  eaftox converts ELAN EAF annotations to interlinear glossed text and
  LaTeX gb4e examples and extracts corresponding audio segments. The
  browser edition processes EAF, WAV, and MP3 files locally without
  uploading them to a server. It provides automatic tier mapping,
  clickable output-tier selection, a live preview, ZIP export, and
  a self-contained HTML file for offline use.
keywords:
  - linguistics
  - ELAN
  - EAF
  - interlinear glossed text
  - audio segmentation
  - language documentation
